<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Crispo family</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1383–<a href="/years/1566">1566</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as House of Crispo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Crispo family were the second dynasty of the Duchy of the Archipelago, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> state centred on Naxos in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a>. Francesco I Crispo seized the duchy in 1383 from the last of the Sanudo line, and his descendants ruled it, mostly under Venetian protection and later as Ottoman tributaries, until Selim II deposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giacomo-iv-crispo">Giacomo IV Crispo</a> in 1566.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/crispo-family.jpg" alt="Crispo family" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: VIGNERON · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crispi_Coat_of_Arms.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
